<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Trucial States</h1><p class="st-meta">1820 CE – 1971 CE · capital Dubai</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British-protected sheikhdoms of the lower Gulf coast, bound by maritime truces from 1820 and united as the UAE in 1971.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After expeditions against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-ras-al-khaimah">Qawasim</a> of the Sheikhdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras-al-khaimah">Ras al-Khaimah</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> imposed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/general-maritime-treaty-of-1820">General Maritime Treaty of 1820</a> on the rulers of the coast. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perpetual-maritime-truce">Perpetual Maritime Truce</a> of 1853 banned warfare at sea, giving the Trucial States, or Trucial Coast, their name, and exclusive agreements in 1892 gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> control of their foreign relations.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Each sheikh governed his own territory; <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> managed defence and foreign affairs through a political agent, based at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sheikhdom-of-sharjah">Sharjah</a> and from 1954 at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-dubai">Dubai</a>. Members were <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-abu-dhabi">Abu Dhabi</a>, Dubai, Sharjah, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-ajman">Ajman</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-umm-al-quwain">Umm al-Quwain</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-ras-al-khaimah">Ras al-Khaimah</a>, later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-fujairah">Fujairah</a> and briefly <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-kalba">Kalba</a>. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trucial-states-council">Trucial States Council</a> from 1952 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trucial-oman-scouts">Trucial Oman Scouts</a> provided common institutions, and oil from 1962 transformed Abu Dhabi.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1968 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> announced its withdrawal from east of Suez. After negotiations, six sheikhdoms formed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a> on 2 December 1971, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-ras-al-khaimah">Ras al-Khaimah</a> joined in 1972.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/trucial-states.jpg" alt="Trucial States" width="320" height="174"><figcaption>Image: Svyatoslav · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Trucial_States_(1968%E2%80%931971).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1820 CE – 1971 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dubai</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Trucial Oman, Trucial Coast, Trucial Sheikhdoms</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1896&amp;focus=trucial-states" aria-label="Trucial States on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6119 1301 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Trucial States lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6439 1557L4997 651M6439 1557L6446 1533M6439 1557L6484 1482M6439 1557L6468 1502M6439 1557L6446 1533M6439 1557L6466 1504M6439 1557L6469 1500M6439 1557L6471 1494M6439 1557L6494 1509M6439 1557L6495 1512"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M6446 1533h0M6484 1482h0M6468 1502h0M6446 1533h0M6466 1504h0M6469 1500h0M6471 1494h0M6494 1509h0M6495 1512h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6439 1557h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6439 1557h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1896&amp;focus=trucial-states">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
